<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oneida Lake</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oneida Lake is the largest lake lying wholly within <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> State, north-east of Syracuse. Its shores and the creeks flowing into it were the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of the Oneida nation of the Iroquois Confederacy, and it lay on the water route linking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohawk-river">Mohawk River</a> to Lake <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ontario">Ontario</a>. It later became part of the New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a> State canal system.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oneida-lake.jpg" alt="Oneida Lake" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joegrimes at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Oneida_Lake_seen_from_Yacht_Club_in_Cicero_New_York.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
